@id=still-to-come-is-marked-where-it-is-written @kind=decision
Feature: What is still to come and what is built are declared where they are written; nothing moves once it is built

  Not a folder for work still to come beside one for built work, nor a change kept in a file of its
  own until it is merged into its feature: a feature or a rule declares its maturity where it is
  written, and `implemented`, the rung above ready, promises that its examples pass. A folder holds
  one dimension well, lifecycle is the one that changes fastest, and a rule is the unit that is
  built. The price is that a feature's file holds rules at different maturities, told apart only by
  their tags, and that what is built says so for as long as it exists.
